From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: check the job's done fence, not the parent, on a timeout

pvr_queue_timedout_job() starts with

	if (dma_fence_is_signaled(s_job->s_fence->parent))
		return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;

(mainline ee7cb7425314, "drm/imagination: Don't timeout job if its fence
has been signaled", carried here through
drm-imagination-carry-the-mainline-driver). Stable has it since 6.18.53 as
2d607646909a, without mainline 2224d6642136, so plain 6.18.53 and 6.18.54 run
it with the old 500 ms timeout. The parent can be NULL at that point, and
dma_fence_is_signaled() does not check for NULL.

WHY THE PARENT CAN BE NULL -- read, 6.18.53 and mainline alike

  drm_sched_run_job_work() calls drm_sched_job_begin() first
  (sched_main.c:1254), which puts the job on pending_list and arms work_tdr
  (sched_main.c:501-508); then run_job() (:1261); only then
  drm_sched_fence_scheduled() stores the parent (:1263, sched_fence.c:65-75).
  drm_sched_job_timedout() hands the first pending job to the driver
  (sched_main.c:537-560). A job whose run_job() has not returned when the
  timeout expires reaches the handler with parent == NULL. The scheduler
  itself treats that as a normal state: drm_sched_stop() tests
  `s_job->s_fence->parent &&` (:629), drm_sched_start() `if (!fence)` (:703).
  Other drivers in the same place: amdgpu's soft recovery checks `!fence`;
  etnaviv tests out_fence, the finished fence it takes at push
  (etnaviv_sched.c:121); panfrost tests the done_fence that run_job() sets
  before anything that can block (panfrost_job.c:401). lima tests
  task->fence, which run_job() sets only after lima_pm_busy() has resumed the
  GPU (lima_sched.c:220/226), so it carries the same class of defect (read,
  not reported).

WHAT WAS SEEN -- one oops, the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-13

  Test kernel 6.18.36-wdtlock, CPU0 soft-locked by LKDTM:
    Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000030
    pc : pvr_queue_timedout_job+0x1c/0x238 [powervr]
  Resolved against the powervr.ko of that kernel: +0x1c is
  `ldr x0, [x20, #48]`, x20 = s_job->s_fence->parent (s_fence at +16 of the
  job, parent at +136 of the fence), 48 = offsetof(struct dma_fence, flags).
  A rebuild of that tree with the same compiler (Debian gcc 12.2.0-14) gives
  the same 142 instruction words, and scripts/faddr2line puts +0x1c at
  pvr_queue.c:873 through dma_fence_is_signaled(). drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/
  and the scheduler are byte-identical between that tree and 6.18.53. The
  handler ran at 76.9 s; with the 60 s timeout (mainline 2224d6642136) the
  timer was last armed at or before 16.9 s, about 3 s after the LKDTM entry
  at 13.8 s.

HOW CPU0 CAN HOLD run_job() -- read, not observed on silicon

  The GPU interrupt is threaded with IRQF_ONESHOT (pvr_device.c:308-310), and
  the thread takes the IRQ's effective affinity (kernel/irq/manage.c:1011-1045).
  If that is the soft-locked CPU, the thread never runs. A runtime suspend
  then waits for it in disable_irq() -> synchronize_irq() (pvr_power.c:126,
  manage.c:115), and the next run_job() waits for that suspend in
  pm_runtime_resume_and_get() (drivers/base/power/runtime.c:826-850). The
  fix does not depend on this chain: any
  run_job() that takes longer than the timeout reaches line 873 with a NULL
  parent.

THE FIX

Test job->done_fence instead. It is the fence run_job() returns as the
parent, the one pvr_queue_timedout_job() and pvr_queue_start() re-assign as
the parent, and pvr_queue_prepare_job() initialises it before the job can
reach the pending list (its comment at pvr_queue.c:582). Where the parent is
set, the two are the same fence and nothing changes. Where it is not, the job
has not been submitted and is not done, so the handler goes on to its
stop/start; drm_sched_stop() there waits for the pending run_job()
(drm_sched_wqueue_stop() -> cancel_work_sync()). If run_job() never returns,
the handler blocks there instead of oopsing, and the hung-task detector
names it. If run_job() failed (an ERR_PTR, e.g. from pvr_job_get_pm_ref()),
the parent stays NULL for good and the done fence unsignalled;
drm_sched_stop() then finds the finished fence already signalled with the
error, takes the job off the pending list and has it freed as the guilty job.

UPSTREAM

pvr_queue.c here is byte-identical to mainline master, linux-next,
drm-misc-next and drm-misc-fixes (2026-09-27). No fix is posted: no
dri-devel patchwork series since 2026-05-01 touches this line. So this is a
mainline defect, not an import artefact, and one stable already ships.
Upstream form: Fixes: ee7cb7425314.

VERIFIED HERE (2026-09-27): applies with --fuzz=0 after the full series on a
fresh 6.18.53; drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/ builds at W=1 with no warning
(cross gcc 16.2.1). The object's handler now loads s_job+184
(= done_fence, measured with offsetof) and tests bit 1 of +48. NOT
hardware-proven.

FALSIFIER, on a test kernel with
a test-only patch (drm-imagination-shorten-the-scheduler-timeout-and-hold-run-job, not carried) and
tdr_selftest_timeout_ms=2000, tdr_selftest_run_job_delay_ms=5000, one GL
client: without this patch an oops in
pvr_queue_timedout_job at address 0x30; with it "Job timeout" after the
"holding" line, then "released", no oops, and the client finishes.

For a comparison run, use a build without this patch.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c
@@ -867,10 +867,17 @@
 	struct drm_gpu_scheduler *sched = s_job->sched;
 	struct pvr_queue *queue = container_of(sched, struct pvr_queue, scheduler);
 	struct pvr_device *pvr_dev = queue->ctx->pvr_dev;
-	struct pvr_job *job;
+	struct pvr_job *job = container_of(s_job, struct pvr_job, base);
 	u32 job_count = 0;
 
-	if (dma_fence_is_signaled(s_job->s_fence->parent))
+	/*
+	 * Not s_fence->parent: drm_sched arms this timeout before it calls
+	 * run_job(), and sets the parent only when run_job() returns, so a job
+	 * whose run_job() has not returned yet arrives here with a NULL parent.
+	 * The done fence is what run_job() returns as the parent, and
+	 * prepare_job() initialises it before the job reaches the pending list.
+	 */
+	if (dma_fence_is_signaled(job->done_fence))
 		return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;
 
 	dev_err(sched->dev, "Job timeout\n");
